%% Sequence — a signal's lifecycle with human-in-the-loop approval. Edit freely.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Cust as Customer
    participant Src as Source (survey/ticket/review)
    participant Ing as Ingestion
    participant LLM as Enrichment + synthesis (LLM)
    participant Eng as Triage graph (governance · approval)
    actor Op as Practitioner
    participant Sys as Execution + audit
    participant Meas as Measurement scheduler
    participant Mem as Learning memory

    Cust->>Src: leaves feedback
    Src->>Ing: signal (connector pull / CSV / JSON)
    Ing->>LLM: enrich (identifiers redacted first)
    LLM->>Eng: theme insight + composite severity
    Eng->>Op: problem candidate (evidence, severity, suggested owner)
    Op-->>Eng: accept / reject candidate
    Eng->>Eng: problem + outcome contract + action proposals + policy checks
    Eng->>Op: approval request per action (Art 14 interrupt)
    Note over Eng,Op: a blocking policy check withholds approval (four-eyes optional)
    Op-->>Eng: approve / reject
    Eng->>Sys: execute approved action (Jira / Slack, draft fallback)
    Sys->>Sys: audit record + evidence-pack hash (Art 12 pattern)
    Sys->>Meas: schedule t7 / window / follow-up checkpoints
    Meas-->>Meas: re-measure from raw signals · ITS readout · evidence grade
    Meas->>Op: loop verdict (loop closed / fix did not land)
    Op-->>Mem: learning conclusion (status, summary, limitations)
    Mem-->>LLM: retrieved on the next similar synthesis (decayed confidence)
